Internet access: Internet Gateway
Private subnet internet access: NAT Gateway
Admin access: Bastion Host
Connect two VPCs: VPC Peering
Connect many VPCs: Transit Gateway
Connect on-premises to AWS (Internet): Site-to-Site VPN
Connect on-premises to AWS (Private line): Direct Connect
Access AWS services privately: VPC Endpoints

VPC Endpoint is used to connect your VPC to AWS services privately without using the Internet or NAT Gateway.

There are two types:

1. Interface Endpoint
- Used for most AWS services.
- Examples: Secrets Manager, SSM, KMS, CloudWatch, ECR.
- It creates an Elastic Network Interface (ENI) inside your VPC.
- Uses AWS PrivateLink.

2. Gateway Endpoint
- Used only for Amazon S3 and DynamoDB.
- It adds a route to the VPC route table.
- No Internet Gateway or NAT Gateway is required.

Interview One-Liner:

VPC Endpoints allow EC2 instances in private subnets to securely access AWS services without going through the public internet. 
Interface Endpoints are used for most AWS services, while Gateway Endpoints are used only for S3 and DynamoDB.
